  "notes": "A docs-site builder ('Quillstack') for a Neovim plugin. The page is shaped by build health: errors, warnings and notices use red, orange and blue in the header status line, the per-page nav badges, the Build tab count, the colored left borders on issue cards, and the uppercase severity pills. Issue cards quote the offending source in monospace, explain the problem in one sentence, offer a one-click 'closest match' fix plus a select of other sections, and link to the source line and to help. Publish is disabled, with a plain-language reason beside it. The setup checklist (4 of 7) ties onboarding to real progress. Single dark segmented toggle (Source/Split/Preview). Very flat: no shadows, 1px #e2e5ea borders, 6-8px radii. The build-issues list has no codebook entry; I filed it as the proposal 'diagnostics-panel'."
